  "title": "Spain's Housing Crisis Sparks Protests as EU and Spain Address Influx",
  "summary": "Spain's housing crisis led to widespread protests, with tens of thousands demanding action after government measures were struck down by the opposition. The EU and Spain are addressing the migrant crisis in Ceuta and North Africa.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Spain’s prime minister, Pedro Sánchez, condemned the influx of 60,000 migrants from Morocco into the Spanish enclave of Ceuta, sparking political and humanitarian tensions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Spain’s government emphasized the need for an EU meeting to address the crisis, while the situation highlighted ongoing migration challenges in North Africa.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tens of thousands of people took to the streets of Madrid and other Spanish cities as they step up demands for action to tackle the housing crisis.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
