      "title": "‘This can’t go on’: tens of thousands protest against housing crisis in Spain",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/03/spain-housing-protest",
      "description": "<p>Demonstrators take to the streets of Madrid ⁠and other Spanish cities ⁠after ​new legislation fails to pass</p><p></p><p>Tens of thousands of people have taken to the streets of Madrid ⁠and other Spanish cities as they step up demands for action to tackle ⁠a mounting housing crisis ⁠after ​government measures were struck down by the opposition.</p><p>Demonstrators on Saturday waved posters calling for a general strike ⁠after the measures drawn up to address mass anger over the eviction of an 87-year-old woman in ⁠Madrid, and other housing issues, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/spanish-right-wing-votes-down-housing-crisis-plans-protest-movement-grows\">were rejected in parliament</a> on ​Friday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/03/spain-housing-protest\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-03T14:19:46"
